From: Dylan Wong <dywong@global.tencent.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 06:13:50 +0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH 3/4] KVM: x86/PVM: soft-gate FSGSBASE/RDTSCP and emulate
 guest user-mode #UD

With the switcher (patch 1) and the emulator (patch 2) handling the absence of
FSGSBASE and RDTSCP, drop the two hard -EOPNOTSUPP gates in
hardware_cap_check() to informational pr_info()s.

The guest vdso getcpu executes RDTSCP in guest *user* mode, but PVM reflects
user-mode #UD straight back to the guest without consulting the emulator. Route
both supervisor- and user-mode #UD through handle_ud(), which emulates the
EmulateOnUD allowlist (now including RDTSCP) and reflects #UD back to the guest
for everything else -- the same behaviour stock VMX/SVM already implement for all
guest #UD.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Wong <dywong@global.tencent.com>
---
 arch/x86/kvm/pvm/pvm.c | 26 +++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kvm/pvm/pvm.c b/arch/x86/kvm/pvm/pvm.c
index c069e5a9a..78f614a91 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kvm/pvm/pvm.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/pvm/pvm.c
@@ -2159,10 +2159,14 @@ static int handle_exit_exception(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu)
 		}
 		return 1;
 	case UD_VECTOR:
-		if (!is_smod(pvm)) {
-			kvm_queue_exception(vcpu, UD_VECTOR);
-			return 1;
-		}
+		/*
+		 * Route both supervisor- and user-mode #UD through handle_ud().
+		 * It emulates only the EmulateOnUD allowlist -- notably RDTSCP,
+		 * so the guest vdso getcpu keeps working on hosts where the CPU
+		 * does not expose RDTSCP -- and reflects #UD back to the guest
+		 * for everything else, preserving the previous behaviour. (Stock
+		 * VMX/SVM likewise handle all guest #UD via handle_ud().)
+		 */
 		return handle_ud(vcpu);
 	case DB_VECTOR:
 		return handle_exit_debug(vcpu);
@@ -3136,14 +3140,12 @@ static int __init hardware_cap_check(void)
 		pr_warn("Support for host FRED is not included yet.\n");
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	}
-	if (!boot_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_FSGSBASE)) {
-		pr_warn("FSGSBASE is required per PVM specification.\n");
-		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
-	}
-	if (!boot_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_RDTSCP)) {
-		pr_warn("RDTSCP is required to support for getcpu in guest vdso.\n");
-		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
-	}
+	if (!boot_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_FSGSBASE))
+		pr_info("FSGSBASE not available; the switcher will use the slower "
+			"MSR-based gsbase switching fallback.\n");
+	if (!boot_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_RDTSCP))
+		pr_info("RDTSCP not available; guest vdso getcpu RDTSCP will be "
+			"trapped and emulated (slower).\n");
 	if (!boot_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_CX16)) {
 		pr_warn("CMPXCHG16B is required for guest.\n");
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
-- 
